From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrice Brissette <pbrisset@cisco.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 15:10:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] bgpd, zebra: Handle EVPN L3MH port-down handoff and recovery

Backport the port-down and port-up neighbor lifecycle from FRRouting
PR #24584 to SONiC's FRR 10.7.1. Use the existing BPP peer delete ZAPI
to identify lost L3 neighbor backing, retain local bindings during
handoff, and preserve eligible peer fallback during local validation.

Use the older dataplane and EVPN attribute APIs on this baseline. Carry
netlink acknowledgment errors back to Zebra for neighbor reconciliation.
Include the ZAPI and Zebra neighbor lifecycle unit tests.

Re-resolve retained RT-2s when the first matching RT-1 copy returns.
Keep local validation independent of RT-2 transmission.

Signed-off-by: Patrice Brissette <pbrisset@cisco.com>
